### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  1. ADMIN AUTH
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 1a. Login  (public — no token needed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@jayarammittai.com",
  "password": "Admin@1234"
}

###

### 1b. Register new admin  (requires existing admin JWT)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "email": "newadmin@jayarammittai.com",
  "password": "NewAdmin@5678"
}

###

### 1c. Refresh tokens  ← send the REFRESH token here
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/auth/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{refreshToken}}

###

### 1d. Logout  (invalidates refresh token in DB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  2. ADMIN PRODUCTS  (all require admin JWT)
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 2a. Create Product  (categorySlug picks/creates the category row)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "categorySlug": "mithai",
  "categoryName": "Mithai",
  "productId": "kaju-katli",
  "name": "Kaju Katli",
  "description": "Premium cashew fudge made with pure ghee",
  "price": 350,
  "stock": 100,
  "images": [
    "https://example.com/images/kaju-katli.jpg"
  ]
}

###

### 2b. List All Products  (flattened across every category, with resolved stock state)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/products
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 2c. Get Single Product by productId slug  (not a UUID — see @productId above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 2d. Update Product  (partial — only send changed fields; catalogue fields only)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "price": 380,
  "stock": 80
}

###

### 2e. Put a product on a temporary hold  (reopens in 24h unless escalated)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}/stock
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "action": "mark_temporary",
  "customMessage": "Back in a day or two!"
}

###

### 2f. Put a product on a scheduled hold  (requires outOfStockUntil)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}/stock
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "action": "mark_scheduled",
  "outOfStockUntil": "2026-12-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "customMessage": "Back for the Diwali batch!"
}

###

### 2g. Discontinue a product permanently
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}/stock
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "action": "mark_permanent"
}

###

### 2h. Restock a product  (returns to in_stock immediately)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}/stock
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "action": "restock",
  "stock": 50
}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  3. PUBLIC CATALOG  (no auth needed)
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 3a. List All Catalog Products
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/products

###

### 3b. Search by categorySlug + productId
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/products/search?categorySlug=desserts&productId=royal-rasamalai

###

### 3c. Search by categorySlug only
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/products/search?categorySlug=mithai

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  4. CUSTOMER AUTH — phone OTP via Supabase Auth
###
###  The code is delivered over WhatsApp by the Supabase "Send SMS" hook
###  (supabase/functions/send-whatsapp-otp). For testing without sending
###  anything, add test numbers + fixed codes under
###  Auth → Providers → Phone and use them below.
###  Phone must be E.164: +<country code><number>.
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 4a. Request OTP  (sends the SMS code)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+919000000001"
}

###

### 4b. Verify OTP  → returns access_token + refresh_token
###     Paste them into @customerToken / @customerRefreshToken above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+919000000001",
  "token": "123456"
}

###

### 4c. Refresh session  (when the access token has expired)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/otp/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{customerRefreshToken}}"
}

###

### 4d. Logout  (ends this customer's session only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  5. ORDERS  (customer login required — see section 4)
###  Every request needs: Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
###  Customers only ever see their own orders.
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 5a. Create Order — full example
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/create
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

{
  "customer": {
    "fullName": "Priya Ramesh",
    "phone": "9876543210",
    "email": "priya@example.com"
  },
  "address": {
    "line1": "12, Gandhi Salai",
    "line2": "Near Marina Beach",
    "city": "Chennai",
    "pincode": "600043"
  },
  "items": [
    { "productId": "royal-rasamalai",       "quantity": 2 },
    { "productId": "tandoori-paneer-tikka", "quantity": 1 }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "upi",
  "idempotencyKey": "order-test-001",
  "customerNotes": "Please pack separately"
}

###

### 5b. Create Order — minimum required fields only
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/create
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

{
  "customer": {
    "fullName": "Arjun Kumar",
    "phone": "9123456780"
  },
  "address": {
    "line1": "45, Anna Nagar",
    "city": "Chennai",
    "pincode": "600075"
  },
  "items": [
    { "productId": "rich-badam-basundi", "quantity": 3 }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "credit_card",
  "idempotencyKey": "order-test-002"
}

###

### 5c. List My Orders  (newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

###

### 5d. Search one of my orders by order number
# Change the date to today's date in YYYY/MM/DD format
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/search?orderNumber=JM-2026/09/28-1
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

###

### 5e. Verify a Razorpay payment  (Checkout's success response, passed on as-is)
###     Orders start as status "pending_payment" / payment_status "pending";
###     5a returns `payment` { keyId, razorpayOrderId, amount (paise) } for Checkout.
###     This marks the order paid + confirmed once the signature checks out.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/razorpay/verify
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

{
  "razorpay_order_id": "order_XXXXXXXXXXXXXX",
  "razorpay_payment_id": "pay_XXXXXXXXXXXXXX",
  "razorpay_signature": "PASTE_SIGNATURE_FROM_CHECKOUT"
}

###
# Razorpay webhook (called by Razorpay, not by you):
#   POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/razorpay/webhook
#   Header x-razorpay-signature; events payment.captured / order.paid / payment.failed

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  REFERENCE
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  productId: any `product_id` from the `products` table
#    (see GET /api/catalog/products), e.g. royal-rasamalai,
#    rich-badam-basundi, tandoori-paneer-tikka. Prices come from the DB.
#
#  Delivery zone: matched from `deliveryzones` by the address pincode
#    (see GET /api/deliveryzones). zoneId is ignored. A pincode that no
#    zone covers is rejected with 400.
#    Charge / ETA / free-delivery threshold: the zone's delivery_charge,
#    estimated_hours and free_delivery columns; if empty, ₹50 / 2h / ₹1000.
#    Subtotal above free_delivery → delivery is free.
#
#  VALID paymentMethod values:
#    debit_card | credit_card | upi | net_banking | sodexo
#


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  6. ADMIN ORDERS  (all require admin JWT)
###
###  STEP 1 → Login via section 1a and paste accessToken above.
###  STEP 2 → Run 6c (List All) to get a real order id.
###  STEP 3 → Paste that id into @orderId above.
###  STEP 4 → Run 6b / 6d as needed.
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 6a. Live Order Queue — all orders, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 6b. Live Order Queue — filter by status
###     Valid: confirmed | preparing | out_for_delivery | delivered | cancelled
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders?status=confirmed
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 6c. Get Single Order by ID  (paste id into @orderId above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 6d. Update Order Status  ← the one you want to test
###     Change "preparing" to any valid status below
###     confirmed → preparing → out_for_delivery → delivered | cancelled
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "status": "preparing"
}

###

### 6e. Mark order as Out for Delivery
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "status": "out_for_delivery"
}

###

### 6f. Mark order as Delivered
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "status": "delivered"
}

###

### 6g. Cancel Order
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "status": "cancelled"
}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  7. ADMIN ANALYTICS  (all require admin JWT)
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 7a. Sales Analytics — all time
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 7b. Sales Analytics — filtered by date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/sales?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 7c. Stock-Outs — default threshold (stock <= 10)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/stock-outs
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 7d. Stock-Outs — custom threshold (stock <= 5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/stock-outs?threshold=5
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 7e. Zone Analytics — all time
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/zones
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###


### 7f. Zone Analytics — filtered by date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/zones?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

